 a small percentage showing classic symptoms.)<|COMPLETE|>", "CEREAL:Cereal is a type of grain that is rich in carbohydrates and includes various species consumed by humans such as wheat, barley, and corn.", "HARINA DE CEREAL:Flour made from cereal grains, primarily used in baking and cooking.", "SENSIBILIDAD AL GLUTEN NO CELIACA:SENSIBILIDAD AL GLUTEN NO CELIACA, or non-celiac gluten sensitivity, is a condition characterized by gastrointestinal symptoms that occur in response to gluten consumption. Unlike celiac disease, individuals with this sensitivity do not exhibit the same diagnostic markers associated with celiac disease. This distinction highlights that while both conditions involve adverse reactions to gluten, they are fundamentally different in their underlying mechanisms and diagnostic criteria.", "CORN:Corn is a cereal grain that is widely used in various food products and is gluten-free.", "BARLEY:Barley is a cereal grain that contains gluten and can trigger symptoms in individuals with celiac disease.", "VITAMINAS DEL GRUPO B:B vitamins are a group of water-soluble vitamins that play important roles in cell metabolism and are found in various cereals.", "SÍNTOMAS EXTRAINTENSTINALES:Extraintestinal symptoms are non-digestive reactions that can occur in individuals with celiac disease, such as fatigue and headaches.", "DIETA LIBRE DE GLUTEN:The \"DIETA LIBRE DE GLUTEN\" refers to a gluten-free diet, which is a dietary regimen that excludes foods containing gluten. This diet is primarily adopted by individuals diagnosed with celiac disease or those who experience gluten sensitivity. Research has shown that a gluten-free diet can also be beneficial for some patients suffering from irritable bowel syndrome and gluten sensitivity, as indicated by clinical trials. It is particularly recommended for patients with celiac disease to help manage and control the symptoms associated with this condition.", "HUMANO:HUMANO refers to humans, who are classified as primates. One notable characteristic of humans is the absence of the enzyme uricase, which results in elevated levels of uric acid in their bodies compared to other mammals. Additionally, humans are susceptible to celiac disease and gluten sensitivity, conditions that can trigger a range of symptoms when gluten is consumed.", "DIABETES MELLITUS 1:La diabetes mellitus tipo 1 es una enfermedad autoinmune que se ha asociado con la enfermedad celíaca, presentando un riesgo mayor en pacientes celíacos.", "ENFERMEDAD DE SJÖGREN:La enfermedad de Sjögren es otra patología autoinmune que puede estar asociada con la enfermedad celíaca.", "INFERTILIDAD:La infertilidad puede ser una complicación en pacientes con enfermedad celíaca, a menudo relacionada con deficiencias nutricionales."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}